## Scope guardrails

- No social features, notifications, or account system unless requested.
- Preserve existing profile data shapes unless a tested migration is included.
- Keep new dependencies minimal and compatible with Vite/Vercel/PWA deployment.
- Cramble's built-in catalog is exactly four daily habits (First Draught,
  Training Yard, Provisioner's Plate, Evening Seal) plus Sunday Sunward Tablet;
  profile-owned custom habits may append to it, but do not add random or
  long-term built-ins without a new request.
- Daily-group cadence may be daily, exact weekdays, current `periodTarget`, or
  legacy `quota`. New custom habits use one configurable model: once per period
  is target 1; several times per period is target x. Periods use chosen days or
  weeks, with exactly one week resetting Sunday and all other custom windows
  anchored to habit creation.
- Store new counted records in `GameState.habitOccurrences`; allow multiple
  same-day records. Award a period target once only at the full count. Partial
  progress has no reward or penalty, supports **Undo one**, and never consumes a
  skip/pass. Preserve legacy boolean quota history and reward semantics.
- Custom definitions live inside their owning `GameState.customHabits`; always
  derive behavior from the merged base-plus-custom catalog.
